Proposed patch, not applied: the A17 review (R7) F3 asks for the typed-audit
input sizing's sha256 and summary inside the registration. The registration
format is closed by shared_generation.parse_registration, a protected file, so
the builder writes the sizing beside the registration instead
(<registration>.sizing.json, naming the registration's sha256) and
`build_api_registrations.py --check` verifies it.

This patch would let a v1 registration carry an optional `input_sizing` block:
the sha256 of the canonical sizing object and the figures the allowance was
checked against. The block is checked against the registration's own limits.
Once it is applied, the builder would set
  registration["input_sizing"] = {"instrument": sizing["instrument"],
      "sha256": sha256(canonical(sizing)), "max_workers": ...,
      "largest_call_input_tokens": max of the three stage figures,
      "aggregate_input_tokens": sizing["aggregate_input_tokens"]}
before parsing. Registrations without a sizing (the chorus profile) would
keep their bytes. shared_generation.py is in ROUTING_CODE, so applying this
moves the v2 routing descriptor's code identity.

